data_2h_tase2
# Phase identity: room-temperature parent 2H-TaSe2, P63/mmc, Z=2.
# Provenance: Brown and Beerntsen, Acta Cryst. 18, 31--36 (1965),
# doi:10.1107/S0365110X65000063; COD 2310532 (CC0):
# https://www.crystallography.net/cod/2310532.cif
# The source 2b/4f sites are expanded in P1 using canonical coordinates. This
# intentionally normalizes rounded COD symops that crystals 1.7 can otherwise
# fail to deduplicate. The low-temperature CDW and 4Hb phases are excluded.
# Odd 00l cancel, making (002) the first allowed basal harmonic.
# The catalog B_ang2=0.6 A^2 is a modeling placeholder, not source-derived.
# Limiting checks: V=sqrt(3)a^2c/2, Ta2Se4, F001=0 and finite F002.
# Validation: 2h-tase2-p63mmc-structure
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M 'P 1'
_symmetry_Int_Tables_number 1
_cell_length_a 3.430
_cell_length_b 3.430
_cell_length_c 12.710
_cell_angle_alpha 90.0
_cell_angle_beta 90.0
_cell_angle_gamma 120.0
